      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A study is presented of the central hemodynamics, renal function and water-salt metabolism in 42 patients with ischemic heart disease and chronic circulatory insufficiency (grades I and II) and revealed a deterioration of these indices in this categories of patients manifested in a retention of sodium, deterioration of central hemodynamics after increase of venous inflow."},
